WEBVTT

00:13:54.371 --> 00:14:01.336
(Applause and cheers)

00:14:01.461 --> 00:14:05.090
You know, we really tried
to bring him here.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.801
But his parole officer,
who is actually really nice,

00:14:07.801 --> 00:14:09.595
he said "JR, you're pushing too much.

00:14:09.595 --> 00:14:11.013
He's not going to Canada.

00:14:11.054 --> 00:14:12.222
Sorry about this.”

00:14:13.056 --> 00:14:14.933
But he knows I'm here talking about it.

00:14:14.933 --> 00:14:17.561
You know, I want to use art as a bridge

00:14:17.561 --> 00:14:19.479
to make people talk to each other.

00:14:19.813 --> 00:14:21.773
I'm not an activist, I'm just an artist.

00:14:21.773 --> 00:14:23.901
I don't try to tell people what to think.

00:14:23.942 --> 00:14:25.903
I just try to make them think.

00:14:25.903 --> 00:14:27.738
And I really see art,

00:14:27.779 --> 00:14:30.115
to me, it's like, it's in the process.